{
  "id": "navigation/deduced_types/04_deduced_templates",
  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "deduced_types",
  "title": "Deduced templates and aliases",
  "summary": "An `auto` deduced as a template specialization reaches the template, or the explicit or partial specialization it selects; one deduced through an alias reaches the alias",
  "prose": "A builtin type or a lambda's closure type has no declaration to reach, and\nthe `auto` of a `new` expression navigates nowhere. A macro spelling `auto`\nnavigates to the macro.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "template <typename T>\nstruct Box {};\n\ntemplate <>\nstruct Box<char> {};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Box<T*> {};\n\nusing Handle = Box<long>;\n\nBox<int> make_box();\nBox<char> make_char_box();\nBox<int*> make_pointer_box();\nHandle make_handle();\n\n#define AUTO auto\n\nvoid use() {\n    auto plain = make_box();\n    auto chars = make_char_box();\n    auto pointers = make_pointer_box();\n    auto handle = make_handle();\n    auto count = 1;\n    auto callback = [] {};\n    Box<int>* allocated = new auto(make_box());\n    [copy = make_box()] {};\n    AUTO spelled = make_box();\n}\n",
